content:
{
  "asset": "P-101 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22120, on the chemically dosed filtered-water line (sodium hypochlorite).",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the reported 3.0 mm/s must be assessed against Figure 3's HF-300 vibration-velocity zones, which are expressed in mm/s RMS on bearing housings. On that measurement basis, 3.0 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is above the 2.8 Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 Zone B/C boundary; it is not in Zone C (4.5–7.1, restricted—plan maintenance) or Zone D (7.1–11.0, damage likely—stop the pump). This reading therefore does not activate SSP-07's immediate-stop rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: treating the reported housing reading of 69 C as the manual's bearing-housing surface temperature, the applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. At 69 C it is within the normal range, 1 C below the normal upper limit and below both alarm and trip. It is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so SSP-07's requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered by this reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry running: approximately 15 minutes dry breached the manual's explicit 'never run dry' requirement for the Plan 11 seal-flush arrangement. The manual identifies seal run dry among the probable causes associated with shaft-seal leakage and specifies seal replacement and an alignment check as corrective actions. No leakage has been seen yet, but that observation does not establish the condition of the seal faces after the dry-run exposure.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Immediate-action decision: neither supplied reading currently meets the documented highest-vibration-zone stop condition or the above-alarm-temperature P1 condition. A controlled P2 corrective-maintenance shutdown is therefore planned for the dry-run seal exposure rather than an emergency stop based on vibration or temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Primary concern: mechanical-seal damage from the approximately 15-minute dry run. Dry running is prohibited, and the troubleshooting table associates seal run dry, worn or cracked seal faces and shaft-seal leakage. Actual seal-face damage remains unconfirmed because no leakage or internal inspection result is reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Additional seal-failure vulnerability: if the original HF3-450 component seal is still installed, this pump is in the SB-2026-014 affected population. Serial HF3-22120 is above HF3-22000, and the bulletin links early HF3-450 failure on these pumps to a revised sleeve tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible contributing alignment defect: shaft misalignment is a documented probable cause associated with seal leakage, so alignment must be checked. No alignment measurement is supplied, and misalignment is not established as the cause of the dry run.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before the planned isolation, inspect for shaft-seal leakage and repeat and record the readings on the documented measurement bases: vibration velocity in mm/s RMS on the bearing housings and bearing temperature on the housing surface. Record the instruments and measurement locations so the limits can be applied unambiguously.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shut down P-101 for the planned work and implement all applicable isolation, line-break and chemical-PPE controls listed in safety_controls before opening the pump or working on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement to remove the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing installation or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment required for loads over 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the mechanical seal and record evidence of dry-run damage. Replace the seal with one pre-set HF3-450B cartridge seal; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. No sleeve-setting measurement is needed to install HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring and measure the scoring depth. Replace the sleeve if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; the pre-set seal's elimination of a sleeve-setting measurement does not eliminate this damage inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Install a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened. During reassembly, tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm; do not use the superseded 25 Nm value. For other fasteners actually disturbed, use Table 5 on lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check pump/shaft alignment after the seal work and perform laser alignment as required to complete the corrective action.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, close and reinstate the pump in accordance with the permit/isolation process, vent and prime the casing, and confirm that the Plan 11 flush arrangement from pump discharge is available. Do not start or operate the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On the controlled post-maintenance run, check for seal leakage and trend bearing-housing vibration and surface temperature against the documented limits. Zone C vibration (4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS) is restricted operation requiring planned maintenance; an indication in Zone D requires immediate stop and notification of the reliability engineer before restart. A bearing temperature above the 80 C alarm limit requires a P1 work order within the shift; the manual's trip limit is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one for the pump's single-seal arrangement. This is the required replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22120; no sleeve-setting measurement is needed for installation.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; one required whenever the casing is opened for the back pull-out/seal work.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; one conditional replacement, to be fitted only if inspection finds scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth. Confirm requirement before installation.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting the line. SSP-07 applies to all site pumps and the work order must list every applicable control.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves: P-101 is one of the filtered-water-line pumps identified as chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting threshold. Obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment; the manual also explicitly requires lifting equipment for this assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration is in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. For the HF-300, Figure 3 identifies Zone D, spanning 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS on the shown axis, as 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The present 3.0 mm/s reading is not in that zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature rises above the manufacturer's alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The applicable HF-300 alarm limit is 80 C, with normal operation up to 70 C and trip at 90 C; the reported 69 C is below the alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prevent recurrence of dry operation: the HF-300 uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and the manual states 'never run dry'. Priming/venting and flush availability are therefore return-to-service checks, not optional steps.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: allow 4.0 task hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: allow 1.5 task hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours, in addition to the seal-replacement allowance when performed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If both listed tasks are performed, their documented allowances total 9.5 technician-hours. The arithmetic sum of task durations is 5.5 hours, but the evidence does not establish this as total elapsed downtime or state that isolation, lifting, inspection and testing are included.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the manual's general parts list identifies HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 says not to fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and to use HF3-450B instead. P-101 is serial HF3-22120, so it is inside the bulletin range, not the below-HF3-22000 population that continues with HF3-450. For work on or after the bulletin's issue date of 14 March 2026, HF3-450B is the applicable part.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gland-torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts on lightly oiled threads, whereas SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because this asset is within the bulletin's serial range and is receiving HF3-450B, use 30 Nm; the manual's 25 Nm value remains associated with the superseded arrangement and pumps below HF3-22000. The other listed Table 5 torques are not changed by the bulletin.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The report does not state whether the 3.0 mm/s vibration reading is RMS or where it was measured, nor explicitly whether 69 C is a bearing-housing surface temperature. Confirm both measurement bases before relying fully on the comparisons.",
    "The installed seal type is unknown: confirm whether HF3-450 is still fitted or HF3-450B has already been installed. Actual seal-face condition and any leakage rate after disassembly or testing are also unknown.",
    "Sleeve scoring depth is unknown. HF3-455 is therefore a conditional part until the sleeve has been inspected and measured against the greater-than-0.1 mm criterion.",
    "No alignment measurement is supplied, so the extent of alignment correction, if any, cannot be determined from the evidence.",
    "Figure 3 does not assign values falling exactly on 2.8, 4.5 or 7.1 mm/s RMS to a zone. This does not affect classification of 3.0 mm/s, but exact-boundary restart or stop decisions require OEM/site clarification.",
    "The evidence gives no acceptable post-repair seal-leakage criterion or required duration for the return-to-service test; obtain the site/OEM acceptance criterion before signing off the work.",
    "SB-2026-014 was issued on 14 March 2026, but the fault report and planned work date are not dated. This order applies the bulletin to current work; for reconstruction of historical work before its issue date, confirm which instructions were then effective.",
    "The bulletin does not state thread preparation or lubrication for its 30 Nm HF3-450B gland torque. Table 5 explicitly specifies lightly oiled threads for its own torque values; confirm the required condition for the new 30 Nm torque rather than assuming it.",
    "The operating cause of loss of prime during tank changeover and the specific procedural or control modification needed to prevent another dry run are not covered by the evidence.",
    "Table 6 does not define whether its task times include isolation, lifting, inspections, gasket/sleeve work, reassembly beyond the named task, or functional testing, so total downtime remains to be confirmed."
  ]
}
